# Use the ChessX UI Template

- All new user-facing pages, forms, dialogs, settings, authentication screens, and management modules must use the existing Apex/ChessX UI template and design system.
- Reuse components from `resources/js/apex/components` and follow the layout, spacing, colors, typography, dark mode, responsive behavior, and modal patterns already used by active ChessX pages.
- Do not send users to Laravel starter-kit UI pages or introduce starter-kit layouts into the visible application.
- When Laravel starter-kit functionality already exists, adapt its backend behavior into the Apex/ChessX interface.
- Keep authorization on the backend and also hide unavailable navigation items, buttons, and actions in the UI.
- Reuse an existing ChessX page or component before creating a new visual pattern.
- Preserve the current Inertia/Laravel integration even when a screen is rendered inside the Apex React shell.

## Example

- Bad: link the Apex header's Profile action to a Laravel starter-kit profile screen.
- Good: build the profile form with Apex components inside the ChessX shell and submit it to the existing Laravel profile endpoint.

Only depart from this rule when the user explicitly asks for a different interface.
